Remove many documents from a LanceDB workspace in a few deletes instead of one per document.

Why: Document.removeDocuments (server/models/documents.js) deletes each document's vectors with
its own LanceDB table.delete, and every delete writes a new table version. Removing a library's
1311 section documents (Reindex in AskFiles, which unembeds every section first) took 289 s on
the owner's Mac, 68 percent of the whole reindex (docs/app.md, Indexing time). The LanceDB
provider gains deleteDocumentsFromNamespace(namespace, docIds), one delete per 1000 vector ids,
and removeDocuments uses it, 500 documents per batch, when the provider has it. Other vector
databases keep the loop as it was. Same rows are removed: the workspace_documents of those paths
in that workspace and their document_vectors.

Paths are relative to upstream/. Apply from the repository root with
  git apply --directory=upstream patches/008-bulk-remove-documents.patch

